meta {
  name: SiteAdmin Upload Template Image
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/siteadmin/uploads/attachment
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{siteAdminToken}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(C:\path\to\logo.png)
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data.url) bru.setEnvVar("attachmentUrl", data.url);
}

docs {
  Upload one **image** for a global (SiteAdmin, tenant-less) PDF template and get
  its public S3 URL. Form field name is **`file`**. Images are stored under the
  legacy **ezhealthtrack** key layout `{env}/global/{YYYY}/{MM}/{DD}/{filename}`
  (`global` takes the tenant position since SiteAdmin templates carry no tenant),
  keeping the file's **original (sanitised) name** plus a short unique suffix
  (e.g. `logo_a1b2c3.png`).

  Accepted types: JPG/JPEG/PNG/WEBP/GIF/SVG only. Max **10 MB**, otherwise 422
  `INVALID_UPLOAD_FILE`. Returns `{ "url": "<public-base>/<bucket>/<key>" }`
  (path-style; stored on DigitalOcean Spaces, or a CDN base via
  `SPACES_PUBLIC_BASE_URL`).

  The SiteAdmin PDF-template editor derives an image **id** from the last path
  segment of that URL (original filename + suffix, e.g. `logo_a1b2c3.png`),
  stores `id → url` in the template's `meta.images`, and hands the user a
  `{{image:<id>}}` token to paste into header/body/footer HTML. For a watermark,
  the URL is stored directly in `meta.watermark_image`. See **SiteAdmin PDF
  Report Templates → Update PDF Report Template**.

  Auth is the SiteAdmin token (requires `master-data:write`). Run **SiteAdmin
  Auth → Login** first so `{{siteAdminToken}}` is set. 500
  `UPLOAD_NOT_CONFIGURED` if the server's AWS_* env is unset.

  Edit the `@file(...)` path to a real image on your machine before sending.
}
